---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import siteConfig from '../config/site';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Service & Fair Use | K-Pop Hangul"
  description="Terms of Service, educational copyright disclaimer, and Fair Use statement for K-Pop Hangul."
>
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-16">
    <div class="bg-white p-8 sm:p-12 rounded-3xl border border-slate-200/80 shadow-sm prose prose-slate max-w-none text-sm leading-relaxed">
      <h1 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-extrabold text-slate-900 tracking-tight mb-2">Terms of Service & Fair Use</h1>
      <p class="text-slate-400 text-xs mb-8">Last Updated: September 2026</p>

      <h2>1. Educational Mission & Fair Use Notice</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>{siteConfig.site.name}</strong> is a non-profit educational and linguistic resource designed specifically to help international language learners study Korean through contemporary music culture.
      </p>
      <div class="p-4 bg-indigo-50 border border-indigo-100 rounded-xl my-4 text-xs text-indigo-900 leading-relaxed">
        <strong>Fair Use Doctrine:</strong> Song lyrics reproduced on this site are limited excerpts (typically chorus hooks or selected verses) presented strictly for the transformative purposes of educational commentary, linguistic critique, grammatical dissection, Romanization instruction, and English translation. All copyrights in the underlying musical compositions, audio recordings, and original Korean lyrics remain the exclusive property of their respective lyricists, composers, performers, and recording labels.
      </div>

      <h2>2. Intellectual Property Rights</h2>
      <p>
        All original educational materials produced by K-Pop Hangul—including grammatical breakdown formulas, custom vocabulary glossaries, phonological sound change guides, and practice quizzes—are protected under international copyright. You may freely use, share, and link to our educational resources for personal, non-commercial language study with appropriate attribution.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Linguistic Accuracy & Disclaimer</h2>
      <p>
        While our editorial staff and linguistic models take meticulous care to provide precise Revised Romanization and idiomatic translations, poetic lyricism often contains metaphorical nuance, slang, or artistic license. The educational content is provided "as is" without warranty of any kind.
      </p>

      <h2>4. External Platform Links & Trademarks</h2>
      <p>
        References to third-party services—including Melon, Spotify, YouTube, Apple Music, or specific entertainment agencies—are made purely for identification, citation, and chart attribution purposes. All trademarks are the property of their respective owners.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Removal Requests</h2>
      <p>
        If you are a copyright holder or authorized representative of any artist featured on this platform and have concerns regarding lyric citation, please contact our editorial team via our <a href={`${base}/contact/`} class="text-indigo-600 underline font-medium">Contact Form</a>. We will promptly review and address all legitimate inquiries.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

